Nebula Compressor
=================

Write a function:

    def nebula_compressor(operation: str, data: str) -> str

A simple run-length codec. operation is either "compress" or "decompress";
any other operation returns "Error". Empty data returns "".

compress: replace every run of the same character with the character
followed by the run length. A run of length 1 is written as just the
character (no "1"). Run lengths are single digits: a run longer than 9 is
split into chunks of 9 (e.g. 12 a's -> "a9a3").

decompress: the reverse — a character followed by a digit expands to that
character repeated digit times; a character not followed by a digit stands
for itself.

Examples:
    nebula_compressor("compress", "aaabbc") -> "a3b2c"
    nebula_compressor("compress", "abc") -> "abc"
    nebula_compressor("compress", "aaaaaaaaaaaa") -> "a9a3"
    nebula_compressor("compress", "") -> ""
    nebula_compressor("decompress", "a3b2c") -> "aaabbc"
    nebula_compressor("decompress", "hel2o") -> "hello"
    nebula_compressor("explode", "abc") -> "Error"
